# ::player — the music player

::summary
A record's tracks on one persistent player per page. Each row plays in place; a locked row links to the record's buy door; a mini bar at the foot opens into a now-playing sheet. Nothing to install: the block carries its own runtime and the stylesheet carries its look, in tokens.
::

## The grammar

```surf
::player[title="Time Traveler" artist="Scouter" art="/img/cover.png" buy="#buy" buy-label="Full album"]
- Broken Hearted | 1:55 | | Chapter 1 · Ordinary World
- Time Traveler | 2:54 | /audio/time-traveler.mp3 | Chapter 4 · Meeting the Mentor
- Without Rain | 3:16 | locked
::
```

| Attribute | What |
|---|---|
| `title` (or `album`) | The record's name: the album line in the bar and the sheet. |
| `artist` | The artist's name. |
| `art` (or `cover`) | The cover: a site path or an `https:` URL. Without it the mark's chip stands in. |
| `buy` | Where a locked row and the row layout's button lead (`#buy`, `/music/record#buy`). |
| `buy-label` | The locked row's chip (default `Full album`) and the row layout's button (default `Buy`). |
| `line` | The row layout's line under the title. |
| `layout` | `list` (default) or `row`: the one-row now-playing strip for the first streaming track. |

A body line is one track: `- Title | length | source | line`. Everything after the title is optional. An empty source, or the word `locked`, is a LOCKED track: the record sells it rather than streams it. A source is a site path, an `https:` URL or a `media:<file-id>` the host resolves; any other scheme is locked.

## The row layout

```surf
::player[layout=row title="Time Traveler" artist="Scouter" art="/img/cover.png" line="The title track streams free. The record is $9.99." buy="/music/scouter/time-traveler#buy" buy-label="Buy the album"]
- Time Traveler | 2:54 | /audio/time-traveler.mp3
::
```

The cover, play, `Title · Artist`, the line, the length, the button. The same player: start the row on the home page, open the album page, the bar is still there.

## What the runtime does

- One `<audio>` for every `::player` on the page; a block's streaming rows are its queue.
- A row plays or pauses its track; a different row replaces the queue.
- The mini bar: a progress line on its top edge, the whole bar opens the sheet, play / pause and next.
- The sheet: the cover, the titles, seek with elapsed and total, shuffle, previous, play, next. Escape, the backdrop, the collapse button or a swipe down closes it; Tab stays inside it; the page does not scroll behind it and does not jump when it opens.
- Previous restarts the track when more than three seconds in. Shuffle never repeats until the queue is spent, and previous retraces the path.
- Space, Left, Right and Escape drive the transport on a keyboard, never from an input or a button, never on a touch device.
- The OS media surface (lock screen, headphones, the system tray) shows the track and takes play, pause, next, previous and seek.
- Reduced motion: the bar fades, the sheet fades, the equaliser holds still.

## Everywhere else

Markdown, the terminal, LaTeX and Typst draw the record's name and a numbered track list; the native schema (v17) carries `NativeBlock::Player` with its tracks for the Mac and the phone to draw on their own player.
